---
import ContentLayout from "../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import EvidenceLinks from "../components/data/EvidenceLinks.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Open by design."
  eyebrow="Licenses / Notices / Privacy"
  description="The project’s licenses, the origins of its visual assets, and what this static website stores in your browser."
>
  <div class="content-split">
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Radivine.</h2>
      <p>
        Radivine is dual-licensed under <strong>MIT OR Apache-2.0</strong>. Read
        the complete{" "}
        <a href={withBase("notices/LICENSE-MIT.txt")}>MIT license</a> and{" "}
        <a href={withBase("notices/LICENSE-APACHE.txt")}>Apache-2.0 license</a>.
        Contributions follow the terms in the repository contribution
        guidelines.
      </p>
      <p>
        The vine branding and application icon assets are original project
        assets under the project license. The website uses the existing symbol
        without recoloring or regenerating it. New website diagram paths are
        illustrations, not native application screenshots.
      </p>
      <h2>Fonts, icons and dependencies.</h2>
      <p>
        The website serves a Latin WOFF2 subset of Inter by Rasmus Andersson
        locally under{" "}
        <a href={withBase("notices/OFL-Inter.txt")}>
          SIL Open Font License 1.1
        </a>
        . The original font remains unchanged.
      </p>
      <p>
        The native application’s bundled Lucide icon subset is documented as
        ISC/MIT in the{" "}
        <a href={`${site.source}/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`}>
          third-party notices
        </a>
        . This website’s radial and feature diagrams are authored SVG; it does
        not redistribute a new Lucide icon package.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website build-tool notices:{" "}
        <a href={withBase("notices/LICENSE-Astro.txt")}>Astro (MIT)</a> and{" "}
        <a href={withBase("notices/LICENSE-Tailwind.txt")}>
          Tailwind CSS (MIT)
        </a>
        . Full native application dependencies and bundled library attributions
        remain in the repository notices.
      </p>
      <EvidenceLinks ids={["notices", "contributing"]} />
    </article>
    <aside class="prose">
      <h2>A static site, a local preference.</h2>
      <p>
        The website adds no analytics, tracking embeds, account system or
        third-party font requests. With JavaScript enabled, it stores your
        chosen theme under <code>radivine:theme</code> in localStorage. Clearing
        that browser entry restores System behavior.
      </p>
      <p>
        Copy buttons write the displayed text to your clipboard only after you
        activate them. If permission is denied or JavaScript is disabled, the
        commands remain selectable. No code here installs Radivine or executes a
        custom action.
      </p>
      <p>
        Downloads and repository links go to GitHub. GitHub handles requests
        under its own policies; the website’s lack of analytics is not a claim
        that a hosting or download provider collects no request data. Hosting
        deployment is a separate project step.
      </p>
      <h2>Media is labeled.</h2>
      <p>
        Current website visuals are conceptual illustrations. Historical
        screenshots and sandbox exports have not been represented as current
        stable desktop captures. Future media must retain source, version,
        environment, kind, caption and license provenance.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
